w: 1.~O_ land of rest, for thee I sigh!_ When will the mo- ment come_
w: 2.~No_ tran- quil joys on earth I know,_ No peace- ful, shelt'- ring dome;_
w: 3.~To_ Je- sus Christ I fled for rest;_ He bade me cease to roam,_
w: 4.~I_ sought at once my Sav- ior's side;_ No more my steps shall roam;_
[V:1] (F/G/) | A A A A | c A (A/G/) F | G3/ F/ G A | F3 ||
w: When_ I shall lay my ar- mor by_ And dwell in peace at home?
w: This_ world's a wil- der- ness of woe,_ This world is not my home.
w: And_ lean for com- fort on His breast_ Till He con- duct me home.
w: With_ Him I'll brave death's chill- ing tide_ And reach my heav'n- ly home.
